--------------------------------------------------
Objective
--------------------------------------------------

Create a new module:

backend/src/modules/tenant-subscription

This module manages the lifecycle of a tenant subscription.

This is NOT a CRUD module.

It represents business workflows.

--------------------------------------------------
Architecture
--------------------------------------------------

Use exactly the same architecture as subscription-plan.

Additionally, introduce a lightweight Domain layer because this module contains business rules and state transitions.

The Domain layer is responsible ONLY for business rules.

The Application Services orchestrate repositories and transactions.

Repositories never contain business logic.

--------------------------------------------------
Folder Structure
--------------------------------------------------

The module should contain something similar to:

tenant-subscription/

    commands/
    controllers/
    domain/
    dtos/
    interfaces/
    mappers/
    repositories/
    services/
    types/
    constants/

Inside domain create classes such as:

TenantSubscriptionDomain

and supporting exceptions/types if needed.

Keep the Domain layer small and focused.

--------------------------------------------------
Business Rules
--------------------------------------------------

All state transition rules must live inside the Domain layer.

Never duplicate transition logic inside Services.

The Domain should expose methods such as:

subscription.subscribe(...)

subscription.changePlan(...)

subscription.suspend()

subscription.resume()

subscription.cancel()

Each method validates whether the transition is allowed.

If not allowed,
throw a Domain Exception.

